      "rdebt.title": "Regression & Test-Debt Explorer",
      "rdebt.desc": "An agile regression suite grows every sprint. Left unmanaged, obsolete and flaky tests pile up \u2014 maintenance cost climbs while the value the suite delivers flattens out. Where the lines cross is test debt. Pruning, quarantine and risk-based selection push that crossover back, or remove it.",
      "rdebt.strategies": "Maintenance strategies:",
      "rdebt.strat.prune": "Prune obsolete tests",
      "rdebt.strat.quarantine": "Quarantine flaky tests",
      "rdebt.strat.riskBased": "Risk-based selection",
      "rdebt.chart.aria": "Line chart of maintenance cost versus suite value across 12 sprints.",
      "rdebt.legend.value": "Value (defects caught)",
      "rdebt.legend.cost": "Maintenance cost",
      "rdebt.stat.size": "tests in suite (sprint 12)",
      "rdebt.stat.flaky": "flaky",
      "rdebt.stat.runtime": "CI runtime",
      "rdebt.verdict.debt": "Test debt: from sprint {n}, maintenance cost overtakes the value the suite delivers.",
      "rdebt.verdict.ok": "No test debt \u2014 value stays ahead of maintenance cost for all 12 sprints.",
      "rdebt.bridge.rbt.title": "Open the Risk-Based Testing Explorer \u2014 risk-based selection is how you keep a growing suite affordable.",
      "rdebt.bridge.flaky.title": "Open the Flaky Diagnosis Explorer \u2014 flaky tests are the biggest single driver of regression-suite debt.",
      "rdebt.quiz.prompt": "A regression test starts failing intermittently \u2014 sometimes red, sometimes green \u2014 with no related code change. What is the best immediate response?",
      "rdebt.quiz.a": "Delete the test at once \u2014 an unreliable test is worthless.",
      "rdebt.quiz.b": "Ignore it; just re-run the pipeline until it goes green.",
      "rdebt.quiz.c": "Quarantine it \u2014 move it out of the blocking suite \u2014 and schedule a fix, so it stops eroding trust in the pipeline.",
      "rdebt.quiz.d": "Block every merge until someone fixes it, however long that takes.",
      "rdebt.quiz.correct": "Correct. Quarantine keeps the flaky test from blocking everyone while preserving the signal; pair it with a scheduled fix so the suite does not rot.",
      "rdebt.quiz.wrong": "Not quite. Deleting loses coverage, ignoring trains the team to distrust red, and blocking all merges halts delivery. Quarantine the test and schedule a fix.",
      "rdebt.lab.prompt": "In your own regression suite, which class of test most deserves pruning \u2014 obsolete feature tests, slow duplicative end-to-end tests, or chronically flaky ones? Estimate the maintenance cost it carries.",
      // BDD / Gherkin Explorer (J1)
      "bdd.title": "BDD / Gherkin Explorer",
      "bdd.desc": "Practice the behavior-driven acceptance flow: Feature \u2192 Scenario \u2192 Step. Switch presets to see how a Scenario Outline + Examples table fans out into parameterized test cases.",
