      // Flaky Test Diagnosis (J8)
      "flx.title": "Flaky Test Diagnosis Explorer",
      "flx.desc": "Build classification fluency. For each failure log, pick the flakiness source it belongs to and read the typical fix. The mistake-bar shows where you still need practice.",
      "flx.progress": "{answered} of {total} answered",
      "flx.score": "score {score} / {answered}",
      "flx.submit": "Submit",
      "flx.fix": "Typical fix",
      "flx.feedback.right": "\u2713 Correct.",
      "flx.feedback.wrong": "\u2717 Not quite \u2014 the canonical cause is {correct}.",
      "flx.taxonomy.title": "Flakiness taxonomy",
      "flx.mistakes.title": "Where you got it wrong",
      "flx.src.timing.label": "Timing",
      "flx.src.timing.fix": "Replace sleep(N) with state-based waits (e.g. element to be enabled).",
      "flx.src.order.label": "Order dependency",
      "flx.src.order.fix": "Make each test set up its own state; isolate global singletons; randomize execution order in CI.",
      "flx.src.async.label": "Async / Polling",
      "flx.src.async.fix": "Await the explicit ready signal; never poll without a deadline.",
      "flx.src.network.label": "Network",
      "flx.src.network.fix": "Mock the offending endpoint or add bounded retries with idempotent requests.",
      "flx.src.animation.label": "Animation",
      "flx.src.animation.fix": "Disable transitions in test mode or await transitionend / aria-busy=false.",
      "flx.src.data.label": "Data pollution",
      "flx.src.data.fix": "Per-test fixtures, deterministic seeds; never share mutable global state.",
      "flx.sample.s1.log": "[error] expected text to equal 'Welcome' but got ''\n  at Login.spec.ts:14\n  fixed wait: setTimeout(500) before assertion",
      "flx.sample.s1.rationale": "A blind setTimeout instead of waiting for the DOM to settle is the textbook timing flake.",
      "flx.sample.s2.log": "[error] Request failed: ECONNRESET https://api.example.com/orders\n  CI us-east-1 \u2013 same test passes locally",
      "flx.sample.s2.rationale": "A transient TCP reset against a live dependency \u2014 the test is coupled to the real network.",
      "flx.sample.s3.log": "[error] Element <button data-testid='confirm-cta'> is not stable\n  CSS transitions on parent: opacity 0.3s, transform 0.5s",
      "flx.sample.s3.rationale": "The element is still mid-animation when Playwright tries to click; classic animation flake.",
      "flx.sample.s4.log": "[error] Promise rejection: 'queue not ready' \n  ingest service emits ready event 80\xB120ms after start; test does not await it",
      "flx.sample.s4.rationale": "Test never waited for the ready signal \u2014 async race against the producer.",
      "flx.sample.s5.log": "[error] expected 1 user with email='alice@example.com', got 3\n  CI shared a seed DB; previous test runs left rows behind",
      "flx.sample.s5.rationale": "Shared mutable fixtures leaking between runs \u2014 the canonical data-pollution flake.",
      "flx.sample.s6.log": "[error] passes when run alone, fails when 'list spec' runs first\n  Both tests mutate the singleton `Settings` instance",
      "flx.sample.s6.rationale": "Pure order dependency \u2014 the test reads global state that a previous test mutated.",
      "flx.sample.s7.log": "[error] click() timed out 5000ms\n  Skeleton loader has opacity transition from 0 to 1 before content appears",
      "flx.sample.s7.rationale": "Skeleton loader is still animating in; Playwright correctly refuses to click an in-transition element.",
      "flx.sample.s8.log": "[error] fetch(/health) timed out 30s\n  CDN failover during deploy; staging hit a stale origin",
      "flx.sample.s8.rationale": "A real network condition exposed during deploy \u2014 classic network flake against a third-party endpoint.",
      "flx.bridge.e2e.title": "Open E2E Journey Explorer \u2014 the same taxonomy appears against per-step risk profiles.",
      "flx.bridge.tqx.title": "Open Test Quality Explorer \u2014 Non-flaky is one of the five engineer-acceptance dimensions.",
      "flx.quiz.prompt": 'Which "fix" is treating a flaky symptom rather than the cause?',
      "flx.quiz.a": "A. Mock the offending endpoint for a Network flake.",
      "flx.quiz.b": "B. Wrap the test in retry(3) and call it done.",
      "flx.quiz.c": "C. Replace a fixed sleep with a state-based wait.",
      "flx.quiz.d": "D. Disable CSS transitions in test mode.",
      "flx.quiz.correct": "Correct! Retry-until-green hides the flake; it does not remove it. The other three options each address the underlying cause.",
      "flx.quiz.wrong": "Not quite. The pure symptom-hiding option is retry(3) \u2014 it makes red turn green without removing the underlying race / pollution.",
      "flx.lab.prompt": "A test passes locally but flakes only on CI. Walk through how you would narrow down which of the six sources is at fault before opening a fix PR.",
